course: dictionary
lesson: 8280
title: Rink: a place to skate
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A rink is a large, flat, smooth place for skating. An ice rink has a frozen surface, and a roller rink has a smooth floor for wheels. «Children go ice skating at a rink in winter.»
explain: Look at the words around rink to understand it. «Skate at a rink: never step onto a frozen pond or lake.» The sentence tells you that a rink is a safe place to skate, and a frozen pond or lake is not.
explain: The words before rink tell you what kind it is. «Ice rink», «skating rink» and «roller rink» each name a rink with a different surface, so check the word in front to learn more.
fact: A rink is a large flat area of ice for skating or playing ice hockey.
fact: A rink can also be a smooth floor for roller skating.
fact: The ice on a rink is kept frozen by cold pipes underneath it.
fact: Wear gloves at a rink, because skate blades are sharp, and wear a helmet when you are learning.
exercise: What is a rink? | A kind of winter hat | *A large, flat area for skating | A deep hole in the ground
exercise: «Skate at a rink: never step onto a frozen pond or lake.» Where is it safe to skate? | On any frozen pond | *On a marked rink | Wherever you see ice | On a lake without asking
exercise: What is the difference between an ice rink and a roller rink? | They are the same | *An ice rink is frozen; a roller rink has a smooth floor | A roller rink is frozen
test: Why must you wear gloves at a rink? | Gloves keep your hands warm only | *Skate blades are sharp and can cut hands | Gloves are not needed on ice | Gloves make you skate faster
test: What should you do after a fall on a rink? | Stop skating for the whole day | Lie still and wait for help | *Get up quickly | Stay down for a long time
exam: «A girl in Calgary heads for the ice rink, puts on her helmet and gloves, and skates only on ice the rink staff say is open.» What does open mean here? | Locked shut | Covered in snow | *Ready and safe for skating | Melted and wet
